hexagon: fuse the conv chain of the verify batch of a draft into GDN_CONV_CHUNK

The cost

A verify batch of speculative decoding holds the last token and the draft,
and it keeps a rollback snapshot of the conv state for each of its tokens:
build_conv_state writes one CPY of the CONCAT for each snapshot group
(n_rs_seq + 1 of them). The conv chain check of htp-gdn-match.h refused a
batch with more than one such CPY, thus each gated delta net layer of a
verify batch ran GET_ROWS, CONCAT, SSM_CONV, SILU and 4 CPYs (the app, a
draft of 3) as separate ops. A prompt ubatch writes one group
(patches/hexagon-spec/0003), thus the prefill was not affected.

The change

- htp-gdn-match.h: the refusal goes. The loop after it checks the window of
  each snapshot slot at any token count (column max(0, n_tokens - g) for slot
  g, which build_conv_state writes) and the even stride of the slots. The
  backend gives GDN_CONV_CHUNK the slots as one span with the slot count and
  the stride, and the kernel writes slot g from its walk over the last
  tokens (patches/hexagon-spec/0001, and the DMA path of this series).
- ggml-hexagon.cpp: graph_optimize asks the scheduler to keep the
  projection of the tokens allocated until the SILU of the chain. Without
  it, ggml-alloc gave the bytes of the projection of a verify batch to the
  output of the chain, and the matcher refused it because the fused op
  reads the projection while it writes its output.
- test-backend-ops: the conv chain case gets n_snap snapshot groups in the
  order of build_conv_state. New cases: the 4B with a draft of 3 tokens in
  place, 8224 channels with a draft of 4, 64 tokens with 4 slots, slots
  past the start of the batch, and a batch shorter than the conv kernel.

patches/hexagon-spec/0005 holds the same change of the matcher without the
allocation dependency, and it is not in patches/series.

The results on the host

The hexhost graphs harness (the host code with a fake DSP, the real graphs
of Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0). A batch of 4 tokens with n_rs_seq 3 (the verify batch
of the app) gives 24 GDN_CONV_CHUNK ops, where it gave 24 CONCAT, 24
SSM_CONV, 24 SILU and 120 CPY ops. The MTP path of the harness (n_rs_seq 4,
a prompt of 8 tokens and a verify batch of 5) gives 48 GDN_CONV_CHUNK ops,
where it gave 24. The op counts of prefill 512 (n_rs_seq 0 and 3), a batch
of 5 tokens with n_rs_seq 3, and decode (n_rs_seq 0 and 3) do not change,
and the HTP0 compute buffer stays at 495.52 MiB in each of them.

The results on the phone

The phone stage gdnk of 2026-09-25 (HTP0) passes the 82 cases of the gated
delta net ops of test-backend-ops with the whole series. The 5 conv chain
cases with snapshot groups are part of them. The stage has no draft, thus
it does not measure the speed of a verify batch.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

